  "summary": {
    "en": "Libyan forces have forced Haftar militia members to surrender at a strategic airbase while continuing artillery attacks on Haftar posts, and Turkish officials have publicly welcomed a motion supporting the troops. An armed group blocked the Hamada oil pipeline for over 20 days, causing losses of more than $30 million. China is re-engaging in Libya with military forces linked to recent business deals. The United Nations introduced laws criminalising child conscription and raising the recruitment age to 18. There were 2 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.",
